        "name": "USN-9027-2",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - x86 architecture;   - Hardware monitoring drivers;   - OCFS2 file system;   - IPv4 networking;   - Ethernet bridge;   - Netfilter;   - XFRM subsystem; (CVE-2025-21656, CVE-2026-63940, CVE-2026-74350, CVE-2026-98432, CVE-2026-99999)",
